module

public import Theory.GroupAction.HalfSizePacking

/-!
# Controlling completions of Lie amalgams

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*, combined
manuscript of 1 March 2004, §F.4, printed pp. 273–299.

The section recognizes small faithful completions (F.4.8), then recognizes
completions satisfying local centralizer conditions (F.4.31). The latter has
an exceptional `L₄(3)` conclusion whose proof continues in §F.5.

The present exports establish the abstract finite counting and fixed-point
arguments of F.4.23(4) and the paragraph following F.4.23: distinct completion
classes will give disjoint half-size subsets of a fixed parameter set. This
forces at most two classes, and any permutation fixing one fixes both.
The construction of those subsets and the recognition theorems are not asserted
by this module.
-/
